  "description_short": "Contemporary dining in Plett's town centre with creative seasonal menus and a welcoming garden atmosphere.",
  "description_long": "Tucked into a charming heritage building on Main Street, The Sanctuary offers a peaceful escape from the bustle of Plettenberg Bay's centre. The restaurant's inviting garden seating and relaxed interior create an atmosphere that lives up to its name, while the kitchen focuses on fresh, seasonal ingredients prepared with creativity and care.\n\nThe menu changes regularly to reflect what's available locally, with dishes that balance contemporary techniques with familiar flavours. Expect well-executed mains, thoughtful vegetarian options, and a decent wine selection. Service is attentive without being fussy, making it equally suited to a casual lunch or a more leisurely dinner.\n\nIts central location makes it an easy stop whether you're exploring Plett's shops or heading to the beaches. The garden tables are particularly pleasant on warm Garden Route evenings, and the atmosphere strikes a nice balance between intimate and approachable.",
